instruction:
You are working in the Go repository checked out at /gin (github.com/gin-gonic/gin v1.8.1). A previous investigation concluded there is exactly one bug in /gin/errors.go:

At line ~94, `Unwrap` is declared with a POINTER receiver while `Error()` (line ~84) is declared with a VALUE receiver:

    // Error implements the error interface.
    func (msg Error) Error() string {
    	return msg.Err.Error()
    }
    ...
    // Unwrap returns the wrapped error, to allow interoperability with errors.Is(), errors.As() and errors.Unwrap()
    func (msg *Error) Unwrap() error {
    	return msg.Err
    }

Because of the pointer receiver, a non-pointer `gin.Error` value does NOT implement `interface{ Unwrap() error }`, so `errors.Unwrap(gin.Error{Err: e})`, `errors.Is(gin.Error{Err: e}, e)`, and `fmt.Errorf("%w", gin.Error{Err: e})` chains all fail to unwrap. The hidden test `TestErrorUnwrap` wraps a VALUE `gin.Error{}` and expects unwrapping to work.

YOUR TASK: apply the minimal fix and verify it.

Steps:
1. `cd /gin && git status && git diff --stat` to see current state (other agents are concurrently editing tree.go / response_writer.go / context.go — DO NOT touch those files, do not revert their changes).
2. Re-read the region: `sed -n '80,100p' /gin/errors.go`.
3. Record the test baseline BEFORE your edit: `cd /gin && go test ./... 2>&1 | tee /tmp/before_tests_err.txt | tail -40`.
4. Apply the surgical edit with `edit_file`: change `func (msg *Error) Unwrap() error {` to `func (msg Error) Unwrap() error {` in /gin/errors.go. Only that one token. Do not reformat anything else.
5. Verify with `cd /gin && git diff errors.go` that the change is exactly that one line.
6. Build and test: `cd /gin && go build ./... && go vet ./... 2>&1 | head; go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -40`. Confirm no previously-passing test now fails (compare to /tmp/before_tests_err.txt).
7. Write a TEMPORARY test file /gin/tmp_unwrap_probe_test.go in package gin containing a test that does:
     inner := errors.New("inner")
     wrapped := fmt.Errorf("wrapped: %w", Error{Err: inner})
     if !errors.Is(wrapped, inner) { t.Fatal("value Error does not unwrap") }
     if errors.Unwrap(Error{Err: inner}) != inner { t.Fatal("Unwrap of value Error failed") }
     // also pointer case
     if !errors.Is(fmt.Errorf("wrapped: %w", &Error{Err: inner}), inner) { t.Fatal("pointer Error does not unwrap") }
   Run `cd /gin && go test -run TmpUnwrapProbe -v ./ 2>&1 | tail -20`. It must PASS.
8. DELETE /gin/tmp_unwrap_probe_test.go afterwards (`rm -f /gin/tmp_unwrap_probe_test.go`) and confirm `git status` shows no new untracked file from you.
9. Re-run `cd /gin && go test ./... 2>&1 | tail -20` one final time.

Report back: the exact diff of errors.go, the probe test result, before/after full-suite results, and confirmation that no pre-existing passing test now fails. Do not edit any *_test.go file that was already in the repo.
